  "scientific_conclusion": [
    "Replacing the divergent logistic likelihood by a finite-moment Gaussian mixture materially reduces every extreme-tail failure relative to V45 and gives lower fixed-step validation NLL in TNG100, SIMBA, and Swift.",
    "The candidate preserves residual RMS and high-k total power in all three domains, and all inverse-CDF and DC-projection integrity checks pass, so the finite-moment likelihood supports the stochastic field body.",
    "The remaining failure is still severe and common-domain: q99.999 is high by 0.33 to 0.42 dex, generated maxima are high by 1.98 to 2.48 dex, and physical mean delta squared is high by factors 27.5 to 520.",
    "The frozen branch therefore requires a train-only audit of Gaussian-mixture PIT extreme quantiles, posterior responsibilities, analytic physical moments, and posterior-predictive moments before any new generator, threshold change, or EAGLE access."
